{
  "text": " Hermes on Herdr. An independent Hermes can receive your messages, but it does not automatically inherit your Herdr sessions pain, socket, or caller context. You trust brilliant coding partners, Codex, Grok, Pi, Claude Code. As your workflow grows, coordination becomes the job. The plugin makes the link explicit. Choose a dedicated Hermes profile you trust, and bind it to your current Herter session. Hermes becomes your M2 with full Herter control in the bound session. It manages Herter. Herter coordinates your coding agents. Hermes already supports Discord, Telegram and Slack. Configure a channel to reach your M2 from outside while Herter control stays local. No SSH, no remote desktop, no VPN TN or Exposed Herter Control Port. Keep the host, Herter and Gateway online. The plugin ties the dedicated Gateway to Herter's life cycle. Pause stays paused until you resume. The monitor TUI shows its state. Herter and Plugin boundaries still apply. Session binding is not an operating system sandbox. Same user terminal permissions remain broad. Let the system manage the talent. Keep your judgment, take your weekend back. Hermes on Herder by Hex Leah I.",
